            <ArticleTitle>Obesity = physical activity + dietary intake + sleep stages + light exposure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/07853890.2014.932921</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Daily levels of physical activity and calories from dietary intake have been the focus of obesity prevention measures. Recent findings have made a twist in the line of thinking. The timing of physical exercise and that of dietary intake are also important to obesity prevention. Night-time sleep and exposure to light are therefore important targets of intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
